import Mettapedia.Languages.MeTTa.Prime.NativeIndexedFamilyNIKAdmittedFlow

/-!
# Request-local NIK selection for complete conversion kernels

An exact interpretation of primitive conversion steps extends uniquely to the
free proof-relevant conversion trees generated by step, reflexivity, symmetry,
and transitivity.  This module turns that theorem into one reusable
maximal-native capability family.

The weaker face realizes a primitive step and otherwise returns the complete
authored path for ordinary fallback.  The stronger face is the universal
structural extension and realizes every conversion constructor.  Both inhabit
one gradual semantic contract; complete-path support is therefore a genuine
strict capability gain rather than a dispatcher priority.

Selection remains request-local.  A complete-path request has one strongest
face, while native proof construction and explicit boundary replay remain
incomparable when no boundary capability is requested.  Thus the construction
does not impose a global numeric tier on NIK's four entry modes.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Mettapedia.Languages.MeTTa.Prime
namespace NativeConversionPathNIKSelection

